 SOLUTION 




a) Using the average rate of change formula above for the endpoints (-1, f(-1)) and ( 2 , f( 2 )) , we obtain the following answer:
\frac{ f( 2 ) - f(-1) }{2 - (-1)}
= \frac{ -18 - 3  }{2 + 1}
= \frac{ -21}{3 } = -7



b) Using the average rate of change formula above for the endpoints (a, f(a)) and ( b , f(b)) , we obtain the following answer:
\frac{ f(b) - f(a) }{b - a}
= \frac{ (-7 b - 4) - (-7 a - 4)  }{b - a}
= \frac{ -7 b  + 7 a}{b-a}
= \frac{ -7 (b-a) }{b-a} = -7



c) Using the average rate of change formula above for the endpoints (x, f(x)) and ( x+h , f(x+h)) , we obtain the following answer:
\frac{ f(x+h) - f(x) }{(x+h) - x}
= \frac{ (-7 (x+h) - 4) - (-7 x - 4)  }{h}
= \frac{ -7 x  - 7 h -4  + 7 x + 4}{h}
= \frac{ -7 h }{h} = -7
